// `decimal2_round_to` within a penny of the top of the range, where rounding UP has nowhere to go.
//
// The largest `Decimal<2>` is $92,233,720,368,547,758.07. Rounded to one place that is
// ...758.10, which is seven pennies past the largest value there is. So it traps —
// `burxt runtime error: arithmetic overflow` — and that is the right answer rather than a gap: the
// alternatives are wrapping to a large NEGATIVE amount, or clamping to a number nobody asked for,
// and both are a wrong answer delivered quietly.
//
// The line before it is the same call one place coarser, which does fit and prints. It is here so
// this fixture proves the trap is about the boundary rather than about the function being broken.
use "../../lib/decimal.bx";

region main {
    print(decimal2_round_to(decimal2_from_cents(9223372036854775807), 0));
    print(decimal2_round_to(decimal2_from_cents(9223372036854775807), 1));
}
